※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4536

※ One value in one place is what a reference names.  An array, a list, a
※ string, a set, a dictionary, a tuple and a result are each already several
※ values or already a place, so a reference to one would be a second way of
※ writing what a value of it is.
※
※ A reference takes the whole of what follows it, so `&u8⟦4⟧` is a reference to
※ an array of four and never an array of four references.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let v: u8⟦4⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 3u8, 4u8⟧
    let r: &u8⟦4⟧ = &v
    let e: u8 = v⟦0⟧
    0u6
